"On a loop, the forces on opposite sides make a couple: torque τ = μ × B with μ = NIA, largest when the loop's plane lies along B and zero when μ lines up with B.",
"A commutator that reverses the current each half turn keeps the torque one way: a DC motor.",
"Students should know the right hand rule for F = qv × B. All views are from above, with B to the right from N to S. The balance sits under the magnet and was zeroed with no current, so it reads the reaction on the magnet in grams. The <strong>Mystery magnet</strong> hides B.",
