"<strong>\"The torque on a loop is largest when it faces the field.\"</strong> When μ ∥ B the torque is zero; it is largest when the loop's plane lies along B.",
"<strong>\"A motor runs on a steady torque.\"</strong> The torque varies through each turn; the rotor's inertia smooths the motion.",
